1
00:00:00,130 --> 00:00:01,093
In 1986,

2
00:00:01,093 --> 00:00:02,291
a Big Mac cost

3
00:00:02,291 --> 00:00:05,410
$1.60 in America.

4
00:00:05,410 --> 00:00:06,112
Today,

5
00:00:06,112 --> 00:00:08,580
it costs $6.22.

6
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:09,417
Almost four

7
00:00:09,417 --> 00:00:10,840
times as much.

8
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:12,020
But a dollar from

9
00:00:12,020 --> 00:00:12,938
1986 isn't worth

10
00:00:12,938 --> 00:00:14,491
a dollar today.

11
00:00:14,491 --> 00:00:15,462
So let's adjust

12
00:00:15,462 --> 00:00:16,760
for inflation.

13
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:17,728
Since 1986,

14
00:00:17,728 --> 00:00:19,307
prices in America

15
00:00:19,307 --> 00:00:21,300
have roughly tripled.

16
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:22,224
Had the Big Mac

17
00:00:22,224 --> 00:00:23,367
just kept pace,

18
00:00:23,367 --> 00:00:24,136
it would cost

19
00:00:24,136 --> 00:00:26,750
about $4.85 today.

20
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:28,880
Until around 2008,

21
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:30,310
the two lines crossed

22
00:00:30,310 --> 00:00:31,490
back and forth.

23
00:00:31,490 --> 00:00:32,530
Since then,

24
00:00:32,530 --> 00:00:33,469
the Big Mac has

25
00:00:33,469 --> 00:00:34,570
stayed ahead.

26
00:00:34,570 --> 00:00:35,333
Even restaurant

27
00:00:35,333 --> 00:00:35,839
prices,

28
00:00:35,839 --> 00:00:36,652
which rose faster

29
00:00:36,652 --> 00:00:37,610
than average,

30
00:00:37,610 --> 00:00:38,366
would only take

31
00:00:38,366 --> 00:00:39,820
it to $5.59.

32
00:00:39,820 --> 00:00:40,610
So the Big Mac

33
00:00:40,610 --> 00:00:41,364
didn't just keep

34
00:00:41,364 --> 00:00:42,670
up with inflation.

35
00:00:42,670 --> 00:00:43,490
It beat it,

36
00:00:43,490 --> 00:00:46,160
by $1.37 a burger.

37
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:47,510
Prices tripled.

38
00:00:48,020 --> 00:00:49,260
The Big Mac nearly

39
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:50,300
quadrupled.
